# Nested border radius

When a rounded child sits inside a padded, rounded parent, radii must stay **concentric**:

```
inner_radius = outer_radius − padding
```

Use the Standard UI radius scale (do not invent one-off `rounded-[Npx]`):

| Token | Size |
|---|---|
| `rounded-2xs` | 2px |
| `rounded-xs` | 4px |
| `rounded-sm` | 6px |
| `rounded-md` | 8px |
| `rounded-lg` | 10px |
| `rounded-xl` | 12px |
| `rounded-2xl` | 16px |

If the result is not an exact step, pick the **nearest lower** token. If the result is ≤ 0, use `rounded-none` (or omit radius).

## Common pairs

| Outer | Padding | Inner |
|---|---|---|
| `rounded-md` (8) | `p-1` (4) | `rounded-xs` (4) |
| `rounded-lg` (10) | `p-0.5` (2) | `rounded-md` (8) |
| `rounded-xl` (12) | `p-1` (4) | `rounded-md` (8) |
| `rounded-xl` (12) | `p-2` (8) | `rounded-xs` (4) |
| `rounded-xl` (12) | `p-1.5` (6) | `rounded-sm` (6) |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — same radius on padded shell and child (curves fight)
<div className="rounded-md border p-1">
  <button className="rounded-md ..." />
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — md shell, p-1, xs child (8 − 4 = 4)
<div className="rounded-md border p-1">
  <button className="rounded-xs ..." />
</div>
```

## When it does not apply

- **Flush nesting** (no padding between curves): child matches parent (e.g. `rounded-b-xl` on the last child of a `rounded-xl` frame).
- **Pill / circular** controls (`rounded-full`) — keep full.
- **Standalone** controls with no rounded padded ancestor — use the control’s default radius (`rounded-md` for buttons/inputs).
